    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0648" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg628"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 5, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> On the 21th of April you were good enough
                    to inform me that the military commission, which investigated the case of Mr.
                    James McHugh had reported that, in their judgment, he should be released. It
                    appears, however, from a letter which I have received from him, that he was
                    still at Fort Lafayette on the 31st ultimo, more than a month afterwards.</p>
                <pb facs="0649" n="629" xml:id="pg629"/>
                <p>I earnestly beg you to call the immediate attention of the proper authorities to
                    the case, and to move them to release Mr. McHugh without further delay.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, with the highest consideration, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
